                    <death when="1818-04-08"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p><persName key="DYS01">George Dyson</persName>'s younger brother.  George Dyson's 
    letters lament Abraham's indolence, but he seems to have worked with <persName key="BAN02">Joseph Banks</persName> in 1810 in 
    a very peculiar operation involving the meticulous sharing out of merino sheep between a group of eminent landowners. He also seems
    to have travelled to Lisbon in 1816 on a business venture. 
  </p>
                    </note>
